instrument wingie
; wingie-proc-caves — the Wingie's own resonators, and some cousins, ringing on line in and played
; from the keys: two caves, strings that tune themselves to what you play, nine resonances tuned
; to the ground, and three metals, one of them following the line's pitch. Line/Mic switch to line.
;
; every scene:
;   fader1 (Mix)     from the line as it is to the resonators
;   fader2 (Decay)   how long they ring
;   fader3 (Volume)  the room behind them, or the scene's extra voice
;   keys1, keys2     tune the left and right resonators and strike them; octave1 / octave2
;                    move each keyboard an octave down or up, as on the stock Wingie
;   mode1            held: they ring for ever (or listen, or take the line's pitch)
;   left LED         the left resonator;  right LED  the right one
; Step through the scenes with a held Mode button and a tap on the other.

two caves
---------
; the left line rings a Wingie cave tuned by the bottom keys, the right line a string tuned by the
; top keys; each key strikes its side. The string's ring is fed a little into the cave, so the two
; sympathise. Play loud and they ring shorter, as a hand damps them. Hold mode2 and the cave keeps
; only its odd modes (hollow, like a clarinet).
the cave is cave 1
the wire is wingie 2 shape=string
the oct1 is transpose
the oct2 is transpose
the ear is follower attack=0.005 release=0.5
the hand is attenuverter amount=-1
the hollow is crossfade
the mixl is crossfade
the mixr is crossfade
the room is reverblite 3 size=0.6
the roomlevel is vca

line.left -> cave
line.right -> wire
line.both -> ear
octave1 -> oct1
keys1.pitch -> oct1.pitch
oct1 -> cave.shift
octave2 -> oct2
keys2.pitch -> oct2.pitch
oct2 -> wire.pitch
keys1.trig -> cave.strike
keys2.trig -> wire.strike
fader2 mode1 -> cave.decay wire.decay
ear -> hand
hand -40> cave.decay wire.decay     ; loud playing damps them
wire ~15> cave
cave -> hollow.a
cave.odd -> hollow.b
mode2 -> hollow.mix
line.left -> mixl.a
hollow -> mixl.b
line.right -> mixr.a
wire -> mixr.b
fader1 -> mixl.mix mixr.mix
hollow wire ~> room
room -> roomlevel
fader3 -> roomlevel.gain
mixl roomlevel -> left
mixr roomlevel -> right
hollow -> lights.left
wire -> lights.right

strings that listen
-------------------
; four sympathetic strings on a chord. A tap on mode1 tunes them to the note the line is singing
; right now (until the next tap); the bottom keys transpose them from there (C as heard, G a
; fifth up). The top keys pick the chord. Every attack in the line knocks a talking drum whose pitch rises with how loud you play,
; and a comb on the top keys rings under both. fader3 how much of the drum.
the strings are sympathetic 2
the ear is pitchtrack
the take is samplehold
the oct1 is transpose
the drum is talkingdrum 2 mode=rise depth=0.5
the env is follower attack=0.002 release=0.1
the hit is trigger length=10
the comb is comb 4
the oct2 is transpose
the drums is vca
the mix is crossfade
the guard is limiter ceiling=0.9

line.both -> strings ear env comb
ear.pitch -> take
mode1.tap -> take.clock
octave1 -> oct1
keys1.pitch -> oct1.pitch
take.held oct1 -> strings.pitch   ; the note it heard, moved by the keys
keys2.key -> strings.chord
fader2 -> strings.decay comb.decay
env.gate -> hit -> drum.strike
line.both -15> drum
octave2 -> oct2
keys2.pitch -> oct2.pitch
oct2 -> comb.pitch
drum -> drums
fader3 -> drums.gain
line.both -> mix.a
strings comb ~> mix.b
drums -> mix.b
fader1 -> mix.mix
mix -> guard -> out
ear.confidence -> lights.left
strings -> lights.right

tuned to the ground
-------------------
; hold mode1 while the line plays (a chord, a room, a record); let go and nine Wingie resonators
; tune to its nine strongest resonances. Then the line rings them, and any key strikes them. Above
; them a granular cloud sings the same rings at the top keys' pitch, its density on fader3.
; Hold mode2 and the cloud freezes.
the ground is listen 1
the sparks are grains 3 samplerate=half window=gauss spread=0.8 size=0.4
the oct2 is transpose
the mix is crossfade
the guardl is limiter ceiling=0.9
the guardr is limiter ceiling=0.9

line.both -> ground
mode1 -> ground.listen
keys1.trig keys2.trig -> ground.strike
fader2 -> ground.decay
ground -> sparks
octave2 -> oct2
keys2.pitch -> oct2.pitch
oct2 -> sparks.pitch
fader3 -> sparks.density
mode2 -> sparks.freeze
line.both -> mix.a
ground -> mix.b
fader1 -> mix.mix
mix sparks.left -> guardl
mix sparks.right -> guardr
guardl -> left
guardr -> right
ground.locked -> lights.left
sparks.left -> lights.right

three metals
------------
; a bar on the bottom keys, a membrane on the top keys, and a cave-shaped resonator that follows
; the pitch the line is playing, so whatever you play is shadowed by a ringing of its own note
; (fader3 how loud). Hold mode1 and the follower keeps the last note it heard; mode2 strikes all three.
the bar is wingie 3 shape=bar
the skin is wingie 1 shape=membrane
the shadow is wingie 2 shape=cave
the ear is pitchtrack
the keep is samplehold
the free is crossfade
the oct1 is transpose
the oct2 is transpose
the third is vca
the mixl is crossfade
the mixr is crossfade
the guardl is limiter ceiling=0.9
the guardr is limiter ceiling=0.9

line.left -> bar
line.right -> skin
line.both -> shadow ear
octave1 -> oct1
keys1.pitch -> oct1.pitch
oct1 -> bar.pitch
octave2 -> oct2
keys2.pitch -> oct2.pitch
oct2 -> skin.pitch
ear.pitch -> keep free.a
keys1.trig -> keep.clock
keep.track -> free.b
mode1 -> free.mix                 ; held: the last note stays
free -> shadow.pitch
keys1.trig mode2 -> bar.strike
keys2.trig mode2 -> skin.strike
mode2 -> shadow.strike
fader2 -> bar.decay skin.decay shadow.decay
shadow -> third
fader3 -> third.gain
line.left -> mixl.a
line.right -> mixr.a
bar third -> mixl.b
skin third -> mixr.b
fader1 -> mixl.mix mixr.mix
mixl -> guardl -> left
mixr -> guardr -> right
bar -> lights.left
skin -> lights.right
